**************************************************************************************************************
**************************************************************************************************************
	STIMULI
**************************************************************************************************************
**************************************************************************************************************
*text digit1...digit16:	are invisible text stimuli (=white) that contain a specified digit (e.g. the first) from the selected digitsequence. 
								These text stimuli are needed to determine the correct response in backward trials 
								(it is, however, also used in forward trials for the same purpose).
*audio_digit1...etc,:		These stimuli are the sound stimuli that present the specified digit from the selected digitsequence to the participants
								(e.g. audio_digit1 presents the first digit in the sequence, audio_digit2 presents the second digit in the sequence etc.)

<text digit1>
/ items = digits
/ select = expressions.1digit
/ txcolor = white
